    {
      "id": "4uu7s47",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to Parliament"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Parliament of India consists of the President, Lok Sabha (House of the People), and Rajya Sabha (Council of States).",
        "Articles 79 to 122 in Part V of the Indian Constitution deal with the organization, composition, duration, officers, procedures, and powers of Parliament.",
        "Lok Sabha represents the people of India directly, whereas Rajya Sabha represents the states and union territories.",
        "Parliament exercises Legislative, Financial, Executive Control, and Judicial powers under the constitutional framework."
      ],
      "id": "kl87tlr"
    },
